{"data": {"id": "bca77f8db25d2525b3551ed3063446fc3363a3be38570947c5dffde6147c3f5c", "lineage": "bca77f8db25d2525b3551ed3063446fc3363a3be38570947c5dffde6147c3f5c", "origin": "sample:3", "parent": null, "source": "def solve(data):\n    nums = data[\"nums\"]\n    \n    # Edge cases\n    if not nums or len(nums) == 1:\n        return []\n    \n    # Find the first element from the end that is smaller than the element before it\n    i = len(nums) - 2\n    while i >= 0 and nums[i] >= nums[i + 1]:\n        i -= 1\n    \n    # If no such element exists, reverse the entire array\n    if i < 0:\n        return sorted(nums)\n    \n    # Find the smallest element from the end that is greater than nums[i]\n    j = len(nums) - 1\n    while nums[j] <= nums[i]:\n        j -= 1\n    \n    # Swap nums[i] and nums[j]\n    nums[i], nums[j] = nums[j], nums[i]\n    \n    # Reverse the subarray from i+1 to the end\n    nums[i + 1:] = reversed(nums[i + 1:])\n    \n    return nums"}, "kind": "candidate", "prev": "11a32d2c73368bd2de2ef0a663685d0b6e6c3f68e4b8a44aa2166e8c2c679c0b", "seq": 22}
